  "administeredBy": "clinician",
  "optionalAssessment": true,
  "directions": "Clinician-administered. Follow the official Indian English administration and scoring instructions. The form assesses orientation to time and place, word registration and recall, serial subtraction, retrograde memory, letter and animal fluency, language tasks, and visuospatial copying and perception. Record each of the five domain subtotals; they sum to 100. The supplied text does not include the picture, dot, letter, or drawing stimuli, so use the official stimulus materials and scoring guide for those tasks. Interpret results with education, language, history, and clinical assessment; a score alone is not a diagnosis.",
